WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.919
User and account artifacts help analysts understand who could access the system and what activity may be tied to specific accounts.

00:00:09.919 --> 00:00:17.193
The /etc/passwd file commonly lists local user accounts, user identifiers, home directories, and default shells.

00:00:17.193 --> 00:00:28.434
It does not usually contain password hashes on modern systems, but it is still valuable for identifying unexpected accounts, service users, and shell-enabled users.

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:36.590
/etc/shadow stores sensitive password-related information at a high level and should be handled carefully under approved authority.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:49.154
Analysts may use it to understand account status, password aging, or whether an account has an unusual authentication state, but it should be protected as sensitive evidence.

00:00:49.154 --> 00:00:56.868
/etc/group can show group membership, which may explain administrative privileges or access to files and services.

00:00:56.868 --> 00:01:07.669
Home directories can contain user-level evidence such as shell configuration, command history, downloads, SSH authorized_keys files, known hosts, application settings, and project files.

00:01:07.669 --> 00:01:14.502
Shell history may show commands associated with an account, but it is not perfect.

00:01:14.502 --> 00:01:22.217
It can be disabled, edited, truncated, overwritten, or shared by multiple people using the same account.

00:01:22.217 --> 00:01:29.491
Treat it as one source to correlate, not absolute proof of who typed a command.

00:01:29.491 --> 00:01:40.291
Sudo usage, account creation, account modification, and privilege changes can appear in authentication logs, system logs, package or configuration records, and file timestamps.

00:01:40.291 --> 00:01:43.157
Analysts should look for consistency.

00:01:43.157 --> 00:01:49.990
If a new account appears in /etc/passwd, do logs show when it was created?

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:55.059
If an SSH key appears, do authentication records show use?

00:01:55.059 --> 00:01:59.688
Good account analysis connects files, logs, permissions, and timelines.
